From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Audit Hub <audit-hub@audit-hub.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:36:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] feat(auth): let admins require a new password at the
 next sign-in

For a password that may have leaked, an admin could only disable the
account or change the password for the person.

POST /api/users/:id/require-password-change (admins only, not for their
own account) sets users.password_change_required_at (nullable: an
expand step) and ends every session and access token at once. The next
sign-in with the right password answers 403 "Password change required"
and sends a reset link (a wrong password still answers 401); the reset
message then says an administrator asked for it, and is not sent to a
disabled account. A completed reset or password change clears it.

The account's page requires it after a confirmation, and the sign-in
page says where to choose the new password.

The users spec's guard against the password hash now checks the hash's
field and value instead of the word "password", which the new field's
name contains.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
