 Enabling it (`disabled: false`) lets the person sign in again with that password; nothing else
 comes back.
 
+### Required password change
+
+For a password that may have leaked, an admin requires a new one from the account's page
+(`POST /api/users/:id/require-password-change`, after confirming; not for their own account,
+which changes it from its account page). In one transaction under the account's lock,
+`users.password_change_required_at` is set, every session ends and `security_version` rises: the
+person is signed out everywhere at once. Their next sign-in with the right password answers 403
+"Password change required" (a wrong one still answers 401, so it tells a guesser nothing) and
+sends a reset link (the outbox limits how many), which says an administrator asked for it. The
+reset, or a password change, clears it. It needs email: without it the person cannot choose the
+new password.
+
 ### Web client
 
